# Native per-expert OpenCL decode: the per-expert kernel reads the checkpoint's
# own expert blocks in the K-loop, so routing-aware expert execution computes
# resident experts on the card (campaign: sub4bit-vram-kernel).
#
# Design:   docs/design-routing-aware-expert-execution.md 2.3a-2.3d, step 3
# Campaign: docs/campaigns/sub4bit-vram-kernel.md
# Gate:     a model with >= 512 experts serves on one card with routing-aware
#           expert execution: only the routed experts computed per token.
#
# Prerequisite patches:
#   0039 — per-expert OCL kernel (moe_expert_swiglu.cl, moe_expert_kernel.patch)
#   0040 — per-expert kernel dispatch integration
#   0043 — native expert formats through the CPU tier
#
# Patch 0043 carried the checkpoint's own IQ3_XXS / IQ4_NL / Q8_0 blocks
# into the fused op and ran every routed expert on the scalar CPU tier, with
# an in-code assert that did so "until the OpenCL decode exists". This patch
# is that decode:
#
#   * moe_expert_swiglu.cl gains the native decode tables (the ones of
#     src/core/gguf_dequant.cpp / tools/q4e/native_blocks.py, llama.cpp
#     ggml-common.h pinned clone 56b9eb28) and two entry points,
#     expert_gate_up_native and expert_down_native, with the same dispatch
#     geometry and argument list as expert_gate_up / expert_down. The weight
#     bytes are decoded per element inside the K-loop; no dequantised row is
#     ever written.
#   * moe_3gemm_swiglu_opt.cpp compiles those stages for a native config,
#     lifts 0043's "native + per-expert dispatch not combined" refusal, and
#     dispatches the native stages for the resident experts while the misses
#     keep going to the CPU tier (patch 0011/0012) exactly as before.
#
# Device-free correctness of the same arithmetic is pinned by
# tools/q4e/native_expert.py + tests/python/test_native_expert_gemv.py in the
# arcint repository (block-scale application, partial-block refusal,
# unknown-format refusal, and a deliberately wrong decode that must be caught).
#
# The native slots' per-tensor strides are the tensor bytes divided by the
# expert count (moe_otd_runtime.cpp expert_tensor_span), so the kernel's
# offsets are INTERMEDIATE_SIZE*HIDDEN_SIZE/{2,4,1,8} by role and format.
# Scales reach the device transposed to [groups, oc] by
# maybe_transpose_scale_zp, exactly as the affine path's scales do; the IQ3_XXS
# sign indices are copied row-major (0043 skips the native zp transpose).
#
# Applied against the pinned runtime, build 2026.4.0-22849-71640275d29, on
# top of patches/0003-0044.

